    "result_text": "The build passes green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), the single handler for `POST /api/owners`.\n\nThe added guard counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today and rejects with **429 Too Many Requests** once that count reaches 100:\n\n```java\nLocalDate today = LocalDate.now();\nlong ownersCreatedToday = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n    .map(Owner::getRegistrationDate)\n    .filter(today::equals)\n    .count();\nif (ownersCreatedToday >= 100) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);\n}\n```\n\nIt's placed right after `registrationDate` is defaulted, so it acts as a top-level quota guard consistent with the controller's existing pattern of returning bare-status `ResponseEntity` values for business-rule rejections (400/409). New owners default their `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()`, so each successful create counts toward the day's total.\n\nThe acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (creates 100 owners, expects the 101st to get 429) and the full suite both pass.",
